# Citation metadata, read by GitHub and by Zenodo when the DOI is minted.
#
# Remaining placeholders to fill in before publishing: the repository URL, and
# the DOI Zenodo issues after the first release. ORCIDs and affiliations can be
# added per author.
#
# Steps:
#   1. Push the repository to GitHub.
#   2. Enable it in Zenodo (zenodo.org -> GitHub -> enable the repository).
#   3. Create a GitHub Release (for example v1.0.0). Zenodo archives it and
#      issues a DOI.
#   4. Add that DOI to the `doi:` field below and to README.md.
#      Cite the concept DOI in the paper: it resolves to the latest version, so
#      later releases remain covered by the same citation.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "RadioRealismNS3_Learn: distilling ns-3 5G-LENA NR-V2X realism into an analytical PC5 model for OMNeT++/Veins"
abstract: >-
  Simulation code comparing 5G NR PC5 (V2V sidelink) channel realism between a
  full-stack ns-3 5G-LENA NR-V2X simulation and an application-layer analytical
  model in OMNeT++/Veins/INET. ns-3 serves as the reference: load-conditioned
  surrogate functions for BLER(SINR), SB-SPS resource collision, half-duplex loss
  and HARQ-inflated channel occupancy are fitted to its traces and applied to the
  analytical model's per-cause loss hooks. The fitted model is evaluated against
  a published-analytical reference across six CAV adoption rates over a shared
  SUMO mobility trace.
type: software
